1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:01,751
Python list indexing

2
00:00:01,751 --> 00:00:02,961
in 40 seconds.

3
00:00:02,961 --> 00:00:04,009
Plus the bug every

4
00:00:04,009 --> 00:00:05,358
beginner hits.

5
00:00:05,358 --> 00:00:06,019
Here's a list

6
00:00:06,019 --> 00:00:07,029
of five numbers.

7
00:00:07,029 --> 00:00:08,850
Each item has a position.

8
00:00:08,850 --> 00:00:09,916
And positions start

9
00:00:09,916 --> 00:00:11,507
at zero, not one.

10
00:00:11,557 --> 00:00:12,554
So nums[2] is

11
00:00:12,554 --> 00:00:13,900
the third item:

12
00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:15,066
30.

13
00:00:15,216 --> 00:00:16,124
Negative indexes

14
00:00:16,124 --> 00:00:17,785
count from the end.

15
00:00:17,785 --> 00:00:19,256
nums[-1] is always

16
00:00:19,256 --> 00:00:20,660
the last item,

17
00:00:20,660 --> 00:00:22,183
whatever the length.

18
00:00:22,333 --> 00:00:23,611
But nums[5]?

19
00:00:23,611 --> 00:00:25,278
There is no position five.

20
00:00:25,278 --> 00:00:27,548
Python raises an IndexError.

21
00:00:27,898 --> 00:00:29,648
Recap: 0 is first,

22
00:00:29,648 --> 00:00:31,119
-1 is last,

23
00:00:31,119 --> 00:00:31,986
and len(nums) is

24
00:00:31,986 --> 00:00:33,522
one past the end.

25
00:00:33,872 --> 00:00:35,426
Next up: slicing.

26
00:00:35,426 --> 00:00:37,296
Follow so you don't miss it.
